00:00:00.056 --> 00:00:05.360
Speaker 1: I want to talk a little bit about the&nbsp;
Dr. Anthony Fauci email story and the reason I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:11.840
haven't spoken about it yet is because I don't see&nbsp;
it as much of a story. But I received a few emails&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.840
over the weekend from people saying, David, what&nbsp;
do you think about the Foushee emails? So let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.280
talk about it a little bit today. Last week, The&nbsp;
Washington Post, as well as by BuzzFeed News,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.400
published a bunch of emails in which Dr. Anthony&nbsp;
Fauci is either the recipient, the sender, or both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.360
involved in a back and forth. And these are from&nbsp;
relatively early in the pandemic, February, March,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.720
April. And the emails were obtained through a FOIA&nbsp;
request. And since these emails were released,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.240
all sorts of conservatives and right wing&nbsp;
media have been saying, wow, these emails are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:48.000
the smoking gun about the misdeeds of Dr.&nbsp;
Anthony Fauci. Rand Paul was talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.600
these emails proving Foushee needs to be removed.&nbsp;
And it has become a big story among the right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.480
Now, I've looked at these emails, not all of&nbsp;
them, because there's 900 pages of emails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.360
but I've looked at the emails that the&nbsp;
right wingers believe are the smoking gun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.240
And the reason I haven't talked about it is&nbsp;
I can't find a smoking gun here. One aspect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:17.360
of the emails is the so-called lab leak theory.&nbsp;
And the idea from the right is the emails prove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.920
that privately Dr. Fauci was acknowledging this&nbsp;
could have come from a lab, this might be manmade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.880
could have come from a Chinese lab, even though&nbsp;
publicly Dr. Fauci was not saying that at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.920
time. That's the claim from the right. I looked&nbsp;
at the emails related to this. You can look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:40.480
at them as well. To me, it only shows that Dr.&nbsp;
Fauci seemed open to people investigating this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:46.880
as he remains today. But he didn't believe at the&nbsp;
time that the evidence pointed in that direction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.680
No such evidence had been presented to him. And&nbsp;
eventually you look in the emails, he gets emails&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.160
from others who start to agree, for example,&nbsp;
the immunologist Christian Anderson, who said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.960
hey, we should maybe look at this. And later&nbsp;
emails Fauci and says it's extremely unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.880
that the lab leak theory is the right one. It&nbsp;
just isn't compelling evidence that what Dr. Fauci&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.840
believed at the time was that the lab leak was&nbsp;
likely and that he was lying publicly. I just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.160
couldn't find evidence of that by looking&nbsp;
at the emails. Second point of controversy&nbsp;&nbsp;

